I had 2 ES45 which had their disks cloned giving a "Bootstrap address 
collision, image loading aborted" during the boot of the standard 
kernel. Genvmunix booted fine.

A search of the 'net produced a few documents indicating that setting 
console_memory_allocation to 'old' would fix the problem. This won't 
work for the ES45.

For the ES45, check the value of heap_expand. It should be set to 
'none'. On these 2 machines it was set to 4MB.

