took me a while but got it solved.  a fresh
installation of 4.0f gives my 2 18gb internal disks an
id of rz16 & rz17.  well, after the  new hard delivery
boots, it sees my disk as rz32 & rz33.  so i changed
to device links for my domains

1)so within /etc/fdmns/root_domain
my root_domain was rz16a --> /dev/rz16a
i relinked it, yielding rz32a --> /dev/rz32a

2)& within /etc/fdmns/usr_domain
my usr_domain was rz16g --> /dev/rz16g
i relinked it, yielding rz32g --> /dev/rz32g

3)this is the tricky one...within /sbin
my swap was swapdefault --> ../dev/rz16b
i relinked it, yielding swapdefault --> ../dev/rz32b

i ran the new hardware delivery again & all went well

