Hi!


As many of you suggested, read the manual...
http://www.legato.com/resources/manuals/

It basically says:
* Install the client software
* Run /usr/opt/networker/bin/networker.cluster on every node in the cluster


Thanks to:
Kevin Jones
Stuart Whitby
and many more...



****************************************************************************
Original question

I have set up a couple of Tru64 v5.1A clusters and every time I wonder what
the correct way of setting up Legato Network client is.
 
Should I set up the client as a cluster service so there is only one node in
the cluster that runs the client and access the client through the cluster
alias (or an alias of it's own?)? 
I am doing that on one cluster and it works fine.
 
Or...
 
Should the client run on all cluster nodes and you backup the cluster alias.
I am doing that too on one of clusters and it works fine.
 
What's supported and/or what's the best solution?
Comments anyone?
 
Regards Klas Erlandsson




