Thanks to Peter Gergen, Dr. Thomas Blinn, Jim Cobabe, Richard Glazier for
there comments and theory behind setld. I believe I have found what is
wrong. Originally I had tried to do the install from my pc using nfs. This
is where I started to get the problems. After rebuilding my test server, I
tried loading webes on using the actual cdrom drive in the server. This has
worked and webes is now installed. 

However I am still in the situation that on one of my live servers, I can
see the subset (just) but can not remove it in order to do a fresh install!

#setld -i  webesbase400    
setld: WEBESBASE400: Unknown subset

However a 
#setld -i | grep -i webesbase400
webesbase400         post-load completed    Compaq Web-Based Enterprise
Service Suite V4.0

And I can't delete the subset because it doens't know about it.

#setld -d webesbase400
setld: WEBESBASE400: not currently installed, cannot delete.
#setld -f -d webesbase400
setld: WEBESBASE400: not currently installed, cannot delete.


Does anyone know how I can get rid of it. It's not just a case of removing
the files in /usr/.smdb. as when you come round to installing it again it
says that it is still loaded. Is there somewhere else that the information
is kept?

Thanks in advance

Steve Copper



