The followings are some tips I find useful in this case:

1. Use TeraTermPro instead of HyperTerminal, because it is much more
transparent.
The most recent version of TTPro can be downloaded from the TTSsh page
at http://www.zip.com.au/~roca/ttssh.html
or from the author's site at
http://hp.vector.co.jp/authors/VA002416/teraterm.html, which indeed is
helpful. 
2. Disconnect the harddisks to stop the boot, which helps me to keep the
system at the SRM level.
3. Garbage indicates an incorrect baud rate. Try resetting it starting
at different rate. In my case, the baud rate was set at 38400.
4. Hit cntrl-c to interrupt the booting process, once baud rate is set
right.
5. Try typing a few "enter" on the main keyboard to get an SRM console
prompt on the graphics head, which is not verified by this case yet.
6, "set console graphics" at SRM prompt.

Thank you all,
Zhiqing


