>From Alan:

Uerf stopped being supported around the time the 4100/4000
class machine came out.  The problem is that the error log
written by your system is a format that uerf(8) can't read,
though the difference is probably subtle.  You want to use
the supported tool, Compaq Analyze.  It is included in the
WEBES kit that is on one of the Associate Product CDROMs.
You might also try DECEvent, which is on the Associated
Product CDROMs.

>From Tom Blinn:

"uerf" is not a supported component fro the ES45 systems.

Install Compaq Analyze (part of the WEBES suite on the AP CD)
and try that.

