My problem was:


>After applying PK2 to Tru64 V5.1A, CAP (Columbia Appletalk Package)
>fail to start.
>
>When executing the following comman during system startup:
>
>/usr/local/cap/aarpd ee1 \*
>
>a Kernel Memory Fault occurs instantly.

This was caused by a bug in the kernel in 5.1a PK2 and is fixed with
the following patch from Compaq/HP:

Patch C 00340.00 - Fix for ether_output() when using packet filter

Thanks to Jeffrey Mogul <Jeff.Mogul@hp.com> for taking care of my
crash dumps and to Compaq Stockholm for providing the patch.

-olle




