Thanks to Tim Mark and Alan who gave me a roadmap where to troubleshoote =
the problem. In the meantime, I interrupted the rmvol by CTRL/C =
(completely safe, the AdvFS domain was then OK) and ran the rmvol again =
during the "heavy system load" period. It ran several times faster than =
during the "system idle" period. Well, it finished and the domain is OK.

The source of the problem could be partly in huge amount of small files =
(about 60,000) but there seems to be a problem somewhere in AdvFS =
routines.

We will initiate an IPMT case to Compaq engineering and as soon as I =
will have a serious result, I will summarize.

