This is the "official" (read - includes the marketing hype) positioning
statement for the 4 fall HP conferences...

The Most Comprehensive Educational, Training, and Peer Networking
Opportunities Ever Available to You!

Looking for a training forum to get a handle on how to leverage products
and
services from the new HP? This fall you will have an incredible set of
qualified conferences to choose from. Whether you're a front-line
technologist or a senior IT manager, whether your expertise lies with
pre-merger HP or Compaq technologies, there's a conference designed for
your
specific needs. The only wrong choice would be to not attend one. We
know
you have questions about the future directions of HP computing - and we
have
the answers you need. Now more than ever, you need the insight and
know-how
readily available only through these events.



HP Enterprise Technical Symposium and Technical Exchange 2002
The Future is Here
October 6-11, St. Louis, MO.

The HP Enterprise Technical Symposium & Encompass Technical Exchange is
the
comprehensive conference focused on the full breadth of HP Technology
for
Technologists. This event is for users of StorageWorks, ProLiant,
OpenVMS,
Tru64 UNIX, HP-UX, Linux, Novell, Oracle and Microsoft Technologies.
This
Symposium program contains in-depth technical breakout sessions,
hands-on
workshops, a HP Technology Exchange Lab, "Meet the Experts" discussions,
NDA/roadmap sessions, and Pre-Symposium Seminars. The Encompass
Technical
Exchange is the trade show that supports the Symposium featuring HP and
HP's
business partners exhibiting technical solutions. Throughout the
conference
program, there will be a special perspective provided for the IT
technologist coming from pre-merger Compaq technology. Hewlett-Packard
and
the Encompass User Group jointly produce the HP Enterprise Technical
Symposium. Conference information is available at
http://www.hpets2002.com.



HP World Conference & Expo 2002
Your Road Map for Growth
September 23 - 27, Los Angeles, CA

The HP World Conference & Expo is the largest solutions-oriented annual
gathering of HP IT professionals. Produced by HP customers, the five-day
event will focus on training seminars, sessions, tutorials, panels, and
networking opportunities covering HP-UX, Linux, Windows, MPE, Storage
Management, Security, .Net, OpenView, IT Management, High Availability,
e3000 Migration, Disaster Recovery, Mobility and Internet Solutions. The
renowned expo will feature more than 150 exhibitors, presenting the
products
and solutions shaping the HP marketplace. Visit http://www.hpworld.com/
for
detailed conference and expo information. HP World 2002 is produced by
Interex - The International Association of Hewlett-Packard Computing
Professionals.



InterWorks 2002
The HP Technical Training Conference
September 23 - 27, Los Angeles, CA

InterWorks 2002 is a technical conference focused for the past 12 years
on
training for the deployment and administration of HP-UX and Linux.
Conference tutorials, seminars and paper presentations will provide
in-depth
training including: advanced kernel tuning techniques, storage and
volume
management including NAS and SAN architectures, software development in
all
major languages, system tuning and optimization, high availability,
infrastructure architecture and design, administration and maintenance
techniques for complex environments and methodology and deployment of
large
computational clusters. InterWorks 2002 is co-located with HP World 2002
Conference & Expo. For more information visit
www.interex.org/interworks.
InterWorks is produced by Interex - The International Association of
Hewlett-Packard Computing Professionals



ITUG Summit 2002
The Best and the Brightest
27-31 October 2002, San Jose, CA

HP NonStop focused IT Professionals should consider the ITUG Summit 2002
their first and best conference choice. The Summit is the leading event
for
technical and product education on high-end business critical solutions,
including NonStop platforms, Zero Latency Enterprise solutions, and
more.
Visit www.itug.org/events/summit02/index.cfm for the latest information
on
this event.



Which Conference Should You Attend?

While each event delivers exceptional value focused on the future with
the
latest information on HP product direction, distinct program benefits
might
help facilitate your decision on which provides the greatest return for
your
organization:

HP World 2002 Conference & Expo provides you solid insight into the new
HP
plus a pre-merger HP specific perspective.

InterWorks, the systems administrator's conference, provides you with
continued training and certification on HP-UX and Linux.

The HP Enterprise Technical Symposium and Technical Exchange strongly
focuses on the new HP and also is being built to meet the specific needs
of
the enterprise computing pre-merger Compaq technologist

The ITUG Summit is tailor-made for professionals involved with HP
NonStop
and related solutions.



The question is not whether you should attend - but which one you should
attend!








--
Jeff Killeen

